<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30004" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnīmen</span></b> ,
		ĭnis, n.
		1. munio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a defence, fortification, rampart, enclosure</i>
				(<b>poet.</b> and in post-class. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munimen ad imbres,</span>”
				<i>a defence against the rains</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 352</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fossas munimine cingere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 212</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">narrat esse locum, solidae tutum munimine
					molis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4, 771</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clausae portae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 6, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horti,</span>”
				<i>a fence, hedge</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 3, 24, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
